// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help surfaces (issue #308)  help matches the snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: si [options] [command]

CLI for ServerlessInsight

Options:
  -V, --version                    output the version number
  -h, --help                       display help for command

Commands:
  login [options]                  authenticate with ServerlessInsight Console
  logout                           revoke API key and clear local credentials
  whoami                           show current login status
  schema [options]                 export the IaC JSON Schema used for
                                   validation (draft-07, self-contained)
  show [options]                   show deployed resources from state
  validate [options]               validate serverless Iac yaml
  diff [options]                   show changes between your config and the live
                                   cloud
  deploy [options]                 deploy serverless Iac yaml
  migrate [options]                Migrate a local/bucket state to the Console
                                   (one-time; run AFTER upgrading every writer
                                   CLI)
  destroy [options]                destroy serverless stack
  local [options]                  run Serverless application locally for
                                   debugging (uses no state backend — no login
                                   or cloud state involved)
  force-unlock [options] <lockId>  manually remove a stuck lock (use with
                                   caution)
  help [command]                   display help for command

Typical workflow:
  si login                                        authenticate, then the profile is stored locally
  si diff -f serverlessinsight.yml -s prod        preview changes before deploying
  si deploy -f serverlessinsight.yml -s prod      deploy the stack
  si show                                         inspect what is deployed
  si destroy                                      tear the stack down

SaaS state commands use Console credentials: run si login once, or pass --si-api-key where the command supports it. Run si <command> --help for the full option list.
"
`;

